            <div xml:id="d170-a3">

                <pb facs="0537" n="479" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg479"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Extract from a private note</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1865-08-28"><hi rendition="#small-caps">August</hi> 28,
                            1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>“Nothing has been easier for me to find out than that Julian J. Berrios was a
                    public employé in Cartagena during three or four months, and that he was
                    governor of Magangue when the revolution broke out in November last.</p>
                <p>“He is now in Ocaña, or somewhere there. To pretend he cannot be found is a * *
                    *.</p>
                <p>“The man was here last summer, driving almost every day in Mrs. or Mr. Nieto’s
                    (the president of the State) carriage.</p>
                <p>“I understand that some kind of trial took place, but that it was hushed up, and
                    was merely a farce to cover and protect the man who ought to have been
                    punished.</p>
                <p>“I should not be surprised if you were now answered that he is gone from Ocaña
                    and cannot be found any more.</p>
                <p>“I make you this proposition: give me the order to carry to you this man, bound
                    hand and foot, and you will have him within two months.</p>
                <p>“I am used to these answers.</p>
                <p>“You must only get the authorization from the executive, that I may take hold of
                    him, and you will see if I do not carry the man to you.”</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am well assured of the truth of the foregoing extract, and communicate it in
                    confidence to his excellency, the secretary of the interior and foreign
                    relations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ALLAN A. BURTON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
